# 6. Real-Time Updates

Implement or repair SSE-based real-time synchronization.

When new telemetry, scans, certificates, assets, findings, or migration events arrive, the relevant pages should automatically update without requiring a full browser refresh.

Examples:

New scan completed
→ asset inventory updates

New certificate discovered
→ PKI Visibility updates

New TLS telemetry received
→ TLS Telemetry updates

New handshake observation
→ Protocol Analytics updates

TLS configuration changed
→ TLS Orchestrator updates

PQC migration completed
→ PQC posture and migration metrics update

Ensure SSE connections have:

* Proper authentication
* Tenant isolation
* Connection lifecycle management
* Reconnection handling
* Backoff
* Cleanup on unmount
* Duplicate-event protection
* Event validation
* Error handling

Avoid unnecessary API requests or duplicate SSE connections.

